Why the split
-------------
The code is meant to be taken and used without ceremony, so it is MIT. The
photographs are someone's own frames of real streets and shopfronts, so they
carry an attribution requirement and a short note about what the licence does
and does not cover. Reading LICENSE-PHOTOS takes a minute and is worth it if
you intend to reproduce a depicted work rather than use a photograph as
reference.
